## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Opus 4.8
- **Short description:** Anthropic’s Claude Opus 4.8 (released May 28, 2026) is a legacy Opus model focused on multi-step coding and agentic collaboration, succeeded by Claude Opus 5.5. Public materials describe benchmark improvements, but specific standalone numeric benchmark values were not clearly extractable from accessible text in this pass.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic Claude API `claude-opus-4-8`; available on Bedrock, Google Cloud, Microsoft Foundry, and Claude Platform on AWS per platform docs. No confirmed OpenCode Zen Free ID (`noFreeId` in local metadata).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released May 28, 2026. Reliable/training knowledge cutoff January 2026 (platform docs).
- **IDs:** `claude-opus-4-8`, `anthropic.claude-opus-4-8` (Bedrock). Local metadata ID `anthropic/claude-opus-4.8`.
- **Context window:** 1M tokens context, 128K max output (300K batch beta supported per docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Paid tier — $5 / 1M input, $25 / 1M output (per docs/announcement).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Anthropic model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

